WEBVTT

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.490
Duel...

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.340
Of course, Kotori!

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.810
I’m suspicious.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.570
Yuma could never defeat me.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.360
But he’s now winning
all his duels.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.360
What’s wrong with that?

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.540
Kattobing works best when he’s losing!

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.910
Losing?

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.370
Maybe Astral really exists.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.190
Hey!

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.610
Good morning, Yu—

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:10.590
...ma?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.090
Why do you have weird
looks on your faces?

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.180
I can’t stand it anymore!

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:27.600
Yuma, I shouldn’t talk
about your taste in fashion, but...

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.860
Yesterday!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.110
Good morning!

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.320
And the day before!

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.890
Good morning!

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.280
And before that!

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.030
Good morning!

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.410
Everyone is laughing at your clothes!

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.440
What are you talking about?

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.120
Look at yourself!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.080
What’s this?

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.050
You didn’t know?

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.890
No, I didn’t!

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.420
Why am I dressed like this?

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.480
This isn’t the only issue!

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.430
You’ve been acting really strange!

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:05.280
You have luxurious lunches.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.020
You’re getting 100% on your tests.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.730
And yesterday...

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.060
Here I go!

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.280
I’m kattobing!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.610
What’s he doing?

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.890
What’s going on?

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.830
Someone, stop me!

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.150
Yeah, I’ve gone through rough times.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.400
Who did this to me?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.810
Someone has been watching you.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.000
What?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.970
Same as yesterday.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.680
Someone entered your room
last night and did something.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.140
If you knew,
why didn’t you tell me?

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.660
You never asked.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:51.150
Since I’m in your room, it’s not weird
if someone else is in your room.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.900
It <i>is</i> weird!

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.070
In that case...

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.360
I’ll find the culprit!

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.070
It’s hard to believe you
when you’re dressed like that.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.130
It’s not my choice!

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:07.040
Whatever. You have
bad taste in fashion.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.230
What do you mean by that?

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.040
What about you?

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.380
I have better taste
than you, Yuma!

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.760
Then show me!

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.500
Gladly!

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.230
I’ll pick clothes
for you this Sunday.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.550
Interesting!

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.390
3pm at the shopping
mall. Got it?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.310
Fine!

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.280
Don’t be late!

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.270
I know!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.090
Thank you.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:55.100
You’re the only ones
who care about me.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.780
It’s this girl!

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:08.510
She’s Kotori Mizuki, the thief who’s trying
to steal something precious from me.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.410
Remember her face.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.880
That’s right!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.070
She’s your prey!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.570
ko-tori

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.570
Because cats eat little birds.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:32.710
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.830
They give color to each day;
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.750
Your kindness was harsh;
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:43.010
Freedom begins by accepting differences;
Dance and create the universe

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:50.390
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:56.920
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:03.490
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:07.370
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.490
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.350
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.670
Everyone is not the same

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.590
That’s the reason for living

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:25.840
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.260
That’s why I never give up;
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.150
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.980
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:42.020
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.070
They give color to each day;
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.450
Your kindness was harsh;
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.120
Freedom begins by accepting differences;
Dance and create the universe

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:06.170
Surprising Cat Deck?!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:06.170
Number 9:

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:06.170
Surprising Cat Deck?!

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.170
I’m late because I was choosing what to wear!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.140
I’m really late!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.600
What’s this?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.940
Sheesh.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.940
She’s late.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.340
What’s with Kotori?

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.040
What’s this?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.040
They emit a sound
that sends chills down my spine.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.880
Are you afraid of cats?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.390
I simply haven’t recorded
it in my observations yet.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.430
Then I’ll tell you.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:55.850
Cats can sense the supernatural,
so maybe they can see you.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.740
No, Yuma.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.010
They’re looking at you.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:03.810
This ribbon...

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.210
It’s Kotori’s.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.280
What?

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.280
“I have taken Kotori Mizuki.
If you want to save her, follow these cats.”

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.280
You have Kotori?

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.870
Damn!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.410
Kotori!

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.960
Kotori!

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.890
What is this place?

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:42.310
Cats...

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.720
Thank you for coming.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.090
Who are you?

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.530
I’m Cathy.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.240
Cathy?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.540
Yes.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.950
Call me Cat.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.340
What’s with her?

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.040
I know her.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.750
She always watched you from afar.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.030
Come to think of it...

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:07.420
Come to think of it?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.910
Nope, I don’t know her.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.170
It’s fine. I’m used to it.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.620
Anyway, where’s Kotori?

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:16.010
Why are you doing this?

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.310
It’s your fault.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.170
That’s why I...

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.730
Just give Kotori back!

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.860
Don’t worry. I’ll give her back.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.860
If you defeat me
in a duel.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.530
Duel?

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.500
But if I win...

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.170
Does she have a Number?

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.380
If she does, you
must win this duel.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.130
You don’t have to
tell me to win!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.610
Let’s duel!

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.240
Duel Disk set!

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.890
D-Gazer set!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:08.190
AR Vision Link complete.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.020
Duel!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.980
Full speed ahead!

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:16.780
I’ll go first.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.910
My turn! I draw!

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:23.120
I activate the spell card
Inviting Cat from my hand.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.790
A spell card already?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.500
Due to this card’s effect,
I add Stray Cat to my hand.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:38.220
Then I activate the Continuous
Spell Cat Meeting from my hand.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.790
Continuous Spell?

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.180
As long as she fulfills the requirements,
she can use the spell over and over.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:49.150
I summon Stray Cat
in attack position.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.780
This activates Cat Meeting’s effect.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:04.480
When Stray Cat is summoned,
Cat Meeting lets me summon another Stray Cat.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.860
Why?

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:10.480
No matter how many 100 ATK
monsters you summon, it’s no big deal.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:11.940
Oh really?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:14.000
I set one card.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.840
I end my turn.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.510
Go ahead and attack.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:22.780
Kotori, I’ll save you.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:24.640
All right!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.480
My turn! I draw!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.730
I summon Achacha Archer!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:39.080
When Achacha Archer is successfully summoned,
you take 500 points of damage!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.080
You’ve pierced my heart!

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.360
Stop talking nonsense!

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.170
Next, I’m going to attack!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.450
Wait, Yuma!

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.490
Her plan is to—

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.590
Be quiet!

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.880
Why are you confused?

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:07.890
Attack that Stray Cat!

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.120
Or the other one!

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.230
Or maybe this one?

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.400
Which one?

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.610
Each cat wants you
to attack it.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:28.330
When Stray Cat is in face-up attack position,
you can’t attack a different monster.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.150
That means... Umm...

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:34.710
You’re caught in a dilemma.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:37.410
The two monsters
are both Stray Cats.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.670
If you select one,
the other’s effect works.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:46.680
Since you can’t attack a monster other than Stray Cat,
you can’t attack either one in the end.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.510
What?

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.410
Kotori...

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.390
Damn!

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.070
What should I do?

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:02.950
Yuma, there’s one way
to get out of this situation.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.240
Be quiet!

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.210
I told you to remain silent!

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:11.750
I’ll rescue Kotori myself!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.240
Kotori, just wait.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.830
You’re dueling me.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.610
All right!

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.340
I know what to do!

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:29.680
I activate the spell card
Flip Flap from my hand!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:34.940
This card lets me change the battle
position of one monster on the field!

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:39.320
I switch the left Stray Cat
to defense position!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.440
Go, Achacha Archer!

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:45.170
Attack the right Stray Cat!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.050
That’s right.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:13:00.440
If you switch one Stray Cat into defense position,
Stray Cat’s effect vanishes.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.670
That lets you attack
the Stray Cat in attack position.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.580
It’s impressive that he
thought of this strategy.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.930
Yuma is different than usual.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:13.870
I’ll rescue you, Kotori!

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:15.560
Why?

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:20.480
Why are you looking at her
when I’m right in front of you?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:23.650
I won’t let you
look away from me!

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.610
Keep looking at me!

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.320
What?

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:31.980
I activate the Quick-Play Spell Mysterious
Cat Transformation during your battle!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:37.290
I can activate this card
when Stray Cat is destroyed in battle.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:41.440
I Special Summon Monster Cat
from my deck, hand or graveyard!

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.220
Monster Cat?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:53.060
When Monster Cat appears, all Level 4-or-below
monsters on your field are destroyed!

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:02.650
And you take 800 points of damage
for every destroyed monster!

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.970
Why aren’t you noticing
my passionate emotions?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.890
Damn!

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.580
I set one card.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.540
I end my turn!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.040
My turn! I draw!

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.710
I activate Monster Cat’s effect.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:29.720
Once per turn, I can add one Stray Cat
from my deck or graveyard to my hand.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:33.560
I summon Stray Cat
from my deck.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.980
There are three Level
1 monsters on her field.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.730
The Number is coming.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.400
Bring it on!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.410
I overlay two Level 1 Stray Cats
and Monster Cat!

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.330
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.610
Xyz Summon!

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:58.970
Come, Twin Tail Cat Lady!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.170
Why doesn’t she use a Number?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:08.300
Twin Tail Cat Lady’s effect activates!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:14.800
Once per turn, it gains 800 ATK
by using an Overlay Unit!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.480
Wait a second!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.070
She has two Overlay Units left.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.110
If she uses them all... Umm...

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:26.160
Adding 1600 equals 3400.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.510
3400?

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.470
Thanks for playing with me.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.700
Is she...

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.910
Wow! You’re incredible!

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:43.380
I’ll make you infatuated with me!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:47.680
A Field Spell changes the world
and the battlefield.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.730
I’ll create this world!

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:52.380
I activate Cat World!

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:56.310
What’s this?

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.210
This is a paradise for cats.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:03.230
A world for me,
you and the cats.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:11.300
In Cat World, Cats gain ATK equal
to their original ATK.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:15.450
2800 ATK?

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.410
Yuma is looking at me.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:23.170
Twin Tail Cat Lady,
make Yuma my prisoner!

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.210
Attack him directly!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.040
Damn!

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:34.470
I flip over my trap
card Pixie Gong!

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:38.970
I can activate this card
when I take a direct attack.

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:44.440
I can Special Summon one Pixie monster
from my deck in attack position!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.960
Come, Joe the Pixie!

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:52.690
Fine. I end my turn.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:56.370
You’re really incredible!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.260
Really?

00:16:58.260 --> 00:16:59.330
Yeah!

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.160
But...

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:05.780
But that’s only
in the dueling world.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:08.320
I’m no good
in the real world.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.290
When I’m near him,
I can’t say anything.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:15.130
He doesn’t even notice me.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.840
He sounds like a bad guy.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:22.050
No matter how many spells
I casted on him, nothing worked.

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:24.230
He wouldn’t notice me.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:29.220
So I thought I could connect
with him through his love of dueling.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.710
Tell him!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.880
Just tell him directly!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.620
Don’t give up
and keep on kattobing!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.780
I’ll cattabing!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.320
I’ll confess my love.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.580
The way I feel
about you is—

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:51.340
My turn! I draw!

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.260
I activate Acorno’s effect!

00:17:55.260 --> 00:18:00.930
I send Pinecono in my hand
to the graveyard to Special Summon Acorno!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:07.100
Next, Pinecono’s effect activates
from the graveyard!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:11.060
When this card is sent to the graveyard,
it’s Special Summoned!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:13.030
Wait a second!

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:14.290
All right!

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.910
I’ll also Xyz Summon
with three monsters!

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:21.740
I overlay Level 1 Joe the Pixie,
Acorno and Pinecono!

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:25.370
With this three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.960
Xyz Summon!

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.710
Appear, Baby Tiragon!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:37.590
Then I summon Gagaga
Magician in attack position!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.840
Gagaga Magician’s effect activates!

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.730
I can change its Level
until the End Phase!

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:48.230
I change Gagaga
Magician to Level 1.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.470
Next, Baby Tiragon’s effect activates!

00:18:52.470 --> 00:19:00.490
By using one Overlay Unit, a Level 1
monster on my field can attack you directly!

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.490
Listen to me—

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:04.840
Gagaga Magician attacks you directly!

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.120
Gagaga Magic!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.560
I’m getting fired up!

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:13.310
Here I go!

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:16.630
Baby Tiragon attacks
Twin Tail Cat Lady!

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:19.590
Yuma, it doesn’t have
enough ATK.

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.280
I know! Don’t worry!

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:26.440
I activate the Quick-Play
Spell Ego Boost from my hand!

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:33.760
With this card, one monster gains
1000 ATK during battle!

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:36.450
I choose Baby Tiragon!

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:40.370
Yuma, my feelings for you—

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:48.540
Then due to Ego Boost’s effect, the monster that battles
against Baby Tiragon returns to its original ATK!

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.210
Yuma, I lov—

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.500
I’m kattobing!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.580
Go, Baby Tiragon!

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.420
Baby Stream!

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:05.890
Why?

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.810
All right! I won!

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:22.450
As I suspected,
it wasn’t a Number.

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:30.400
Hey.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.200
Are you okay?

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:38.770
Tell me where Kotori is.

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:47.710
The kittens... tripped!

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:52.350
So cute!

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.560
The kittens... tripped!

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.280
Kotori!

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.400
Yuma!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.070
What are you doing?

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:14.830
The cats wanted me to play with them,
so I couldn’t refuse!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.540
How long are you
going to stay angry?

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.180
I’m not angry!

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:21.460
See? You’re angry.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.200
Umm...

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.840
Umm... Good morning...

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.540
Hey!

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:33.180
Who was she again?

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.660
How rude!

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:38.640
She’s in our class.
Her name is... Umm...

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.580
Cathy. Or Cat.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.320
She’s good at dueling!

00:21:44.310 --> 00:21:47.160
Oh really? I didn’t know that.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:51.120
By the way, did you find the culprit
who was pulling pranks on you?

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.870
Not at all!

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:55.720
I’m going on ahead!

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:58.730
Hey, Kotori?

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:08.370
Observation #11: Yuma still can’t
understand a woman’s feelings.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:15.490
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.490 --> 00:22:17.960
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:20.440
Which one can you activate
from your hand?

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:24.610
A spell card
or a trap card?

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.830
Today’s test is hard;
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:39.960
I want to go home and watch TV;
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:54.430
Anyway, tests are hard; Language,
math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:59.570
Average scores in science
and social studies; I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:01.980
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:04.610
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:07.290
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.900
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.590
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:18.120
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:23.530
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.530 --> 00:23:28.170
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:33.300
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.100
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:43.060
You’re... Shark!

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:46.070
He’s hanging out
with a bad crowd.

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:47.860
Let’s go home, Yuma!

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.660
Why are you giving
up on dueling?

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.450
So you’re going to battle
that boy again.

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:57.000
Shark, you shouldn’t
hang out with them.

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:03.120
I’ll win this duel without using a Number
and bring you back to our world!

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:10.090
Shark’s Counterattack!

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:07.080
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Shark’s Counterattack!”

00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:10.090
I’m kattobing!

00:24:12.320 --> 00:24:15.800
The answer is... a spell card!

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:21.150
Spell cards are useful cards
that you can use from your hand.

00:24:21.150 --> 00:24:23.100
Remember that!
